{% from "macros.njk" import callout, snippet with context %}

{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>A bottom sheet presents choices or a compact task in the context the user
     is already in — it rises from the bottom edge, keeps that context visible
     behind a scrim, and returns as soon as the choice is made.</p>
  <h3>Do use it for</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Choosing from a set</strong> — sort order, account picker,
        "add to" destinations. The canonical sheet is a vertical option
        list.</li>
    <li><strong>Compact forms</strong> — "new label", quick compose, a filter
        with two or three controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Details that shouldn't navigate</strong> — long metadata or an
        "about" panel that belongs to the current screen.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it for</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Destructive or blocking decisions</strong> — "delete
        everything?" is a <a href="dialog.html">dialog</a> territory; a sheet
        implies "this is still the same task".</li>
    <li><strong>Full-screen forms</strong> — real compose and settings
        sub-pages are the dialog's <code>--fullscreen</code> type.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback</strong> — "Message sent" is a snackbar, never a
        sheet.</li>
  </ul>
  {{ callout({
    variant: "info",
    title: "The handle is a glyph, not a gesture",
    text: "The drag handle is drawn (32×4px, static). Drag-to-dismiss is not supported and not claimed — sheets close on scrim tap, Escape or their own actions, like every other overlay here. On desktop (≥600px) the sheet becomes a 560px card docked to the bottom edge instead of a full-bleed tray.",
    href: "dialog.html",
    linkText: "Dialog component"
  }) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-anatomy">Anatomy</h2>
  <div class="docs-anatomy">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 600 260" role="img" aria-label="Bottom sheet anatomy diagram">
      <!-- screen behind -->
      <rect x="1" y="1" width="598" height="258" fill="#5f6368" opacity="0.12"/>
      <!-- sheet docked to bottom -->
      <rect x="40" y="110" width="520" height="150" rx="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <!-- handle -->
      <rect x="280" y="120" width="40" height="4" rx="2" fill="#5f6368"/>
      <!-- title -->
      <rect x="60" y="136" width="110" height="10" rx="5" fill="#1f1f1f"/>
      <!-- option rows -->
      <rect x="60" y="158" width="200" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <rect x="60" y="178" width="170" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <rect x="60" y="198" width="190" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <!-- action -->
      <rect x="480" y="222" width="60" height="20" rx="4" fill="#1a73e8"/>
      <!-- callouts -->
      <g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="700">
        <g><circle cx="300" cy="100" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="300" y="104" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="30" cy="140" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="30" y="144" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="300" cy="180" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="300" y="184" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="300" cy="232" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="300" y="236" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Handle</strong> — the static 32×4 glyph; decorative
          (<code>aria-hidden</code>), no drag behavior.</li>
      <li><strong>Title</strong> — short, 16px/500; optional for pure option
          lists where the rows are self-describing.</li>
      <li><strong>Body</strong> — option rows, fields or long content;
          scrolls while the title stays pinned. Option rows reuse the dialog
          family's <code>fl-dialog__option</code> (48px, state layer).</li>
      <li><strong>Actions</strong> — right-aligned, same button idiom as the
          dialog; often unnecessary for pure pick-one lists.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Same overlay contract as the dialog:</strong>
        <code>data-fl-open="sheet-id"</code> opens it,
        <code>data-fl-close</code> inside closes it, and
        <code>&lt;form method="dialog"&gt;</code> records the pressed row or
        button in <code>dialog.returnValue</code> — picking "Unread first"
        from the sort sheet returns <code>"unread"</code> with zero
        JavaScript.</li>
    <li><strong>Dismissal:</strong> Escape and scrim clicks close it (native
        <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>); focus returns to the invoker on every
        close path. As with the dialog: if the body scrolls, Chromium may
        focus the scroll region first — set <code>autofocus</code> on the
        control that should receive initial focus (the demos do).</li>
    <li><strong>Scroll:</strong> the body scrolls inside the surface (capped
        at <code>min(86vh, 640px)</code>); handle and title stay pinned.</li>
    <li><strong>Responsive width:</strong> full-bleed below 600px; a 560px
        bottom-docked card above.</li>
    <li><strong>Stacking:</strong> a <a href="dialog.html">dialog</a> can open
        over the sheet — the top layer stacks in DOM order and Escape peels
        only the top one.</li>
    <li><strong>Scroll lock:</strong> the page locks while any overlay is
        open — one CSS rule shared across dialog, sheet and drawer.</li>
    <li><strong>Animation:</strong> slides up on open, fades out on close —
        CSS only, <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> disables it.</li>
    <li><strong>No-JS fallback (honest):</strong> without flint.js the sheet
        stays hidden and the page keeps working. Call <code>showModal()</code>
        yourself with one line, or drive it from your own code. See the
        <a href="overlay.html">overlay infra demo</a> for the raw lifecycle.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give the sheet <code>aria-labelledby</code> pointing at its title
        (skip this only when there is deliberately no title and the rows are
        self-describing).</li>
    <li>The handle is decorative — mark it <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> so
        screen readers don't announce a "drag" affordance that doesn't
        exist.</li>
    <li>Option rows are real <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>s or
        <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>+input pairs — native focus, native
        activation, no <code>tabindex</code> games.</li>
    <li>The inert background is native: nothing behind the sheet is focusable
        or announced while it's open.</li>
    <li>Don't remove the focus ring; the global <code>:focus-visible</code>
        ring is what makes the modal boundary visible to keyboard users.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

